Z||000004||Oreif||04-27-2000||02:41 PM||||First, the 2.8L in the S-10/S-15 4WD trucks are the ones with crankshaft problems. This happened due to premature wear of the main bearings and the stress of driving a trans and transfer case in 4WD. The crank in the Fiero 2.8's should hold together up to &gt;200hp. As for The Grand Am you mention, I don't recall any year Grand Am having a 2.8L in it. The first grand am's (1985) had a 3.0L buick V-6 that had numerous reliability problems (Had one for a year then bought my first Fiero!) then they switched to the Quad4 engine until they changed the body style and used the 3.1L. ||||reg||1
